Pipeline Documentation: Purpose and Rationale

Why This Pipeline needed?

Enable Reliable Data Analytics:
The pipeline is designed to transform raw data sources into structured, high-quality datasets. This enables robust analytics, reporting, and data-driven decision-making for the business.

Support Scalable Data Engineering:
By implementing the medallion architecture (Raw → Bronze → Silver → Gold), the pipeline ensures data is incrementally refined, improving quality at each stage.

Automate and Standardize Data Operations:
Automated orchestration (via Azure Data Factory and Databricks) reduces manual intervention, minimizes errors, and ensures consistent, repeatable data processing across environments.

Facilitate Compliance and Governance:
Centralized configuration and infrastructure-as-code practices ensure that deployments are auditable, secure, and compliant with organizational standards.

Accelerate Business Insights:
The gold layer delivers curated, business-focused datasets, enabling faster and more accurate reporting, analytics using such as Power BI dashboard for leadership.

Business Value
Faster Time-to-Market:
Streamlined data flows and automated deployments.

Data Quality:
Each layer of the medallion architecture adds value—raw data is preserved, bronze provides structure, silver ensures quality, and gold delivers actionable insights.

Operational Efficiency:
Automated CI/CD and modular design reduce operational overhead and support rapid iteration. The code is organized with maximum reusability and easy to extend additinal features in future.